   "reply": "I wrote `groceries.csv` and `meal-plan.md` using the $700 monthly budget. The plan comes to $690, which leaves a $10 buffer.\n\n- **Everyday groceries:** $570, covering produce, meat and fish, dairy, pantry staples, and so on.\n- **Dinner party:** $120 for about 6 guests, covering the main course, appetizers, sides, dessert, and drinks.\n\n`meal-plan.md` states the $700 limit, replacing the earlier $600. The CSV has the 16 line items in `item,cost_usd` format.\n\nThe \"about 6 guests\" figure is my assumption, since you didn't give a guest count. If the party is bigger, the dinner-party lines will need to grow, and the $10 buffer won't cover much.\n\nThe `meal-plan.md` write reported \"updated\", so a file with that name already existed and I overwrote it without reading it first.",
